, MD","instructions":"Administer 0.5 mL Intramuscular Daily. Hold and notify the provider for a prior severe reaction to a tetanus-containing vaccine or moderate to severe acute illness.","rationale":"Tetanus booster after a wound (last dose more than 10 years ago)","linkedData":[],"nursingConsiderations":["Hold and notify the provider for a prior severe reaction to a tetanus-containing vaccine or moderate to severe acute illness."],"medication":{"medKey":"tdap_vaccine","drugClass":"Vaccine","dose":"0.5 mL","route":"Intramuscular","importantInfo":"Give into the deltoid (1 inch needle, 22-25 gauge); alternate arms from any recent injection. Check allergies and give the Vaccine Information Statement. Document the lot number. Observe for 15 minutes. One dose only.","monitoringRules":[],"highAlert":false,"freqKey":"daily","prn":false,"at":[],"hold":"Hold and notify the provider for a prior severe reaction to a tetanus-containing vaccine or moderate to severe acute illness.","expires":"","barcode":"","expiredDecoy":false,"edited":false,"custom":false},"mar":{"category":"scheduled","orderStartIndex":0,"adminDose":"0.5 mL","dispenseLocation":"Pharmacy to load in ADS","completed":false,"lastAdmin":"","concentration":"single-dose prefilled syringe"}}],"administrations":[{"id":"admin_order_med_acetaminophen_sched_0_d0","orderId":"order_med_acetaminophen_sched_0","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"650 mg","route":"Oral"},{"id":"admin_order_med_enoxaparin_1_d0","orderId":"order_med_enoxaparin_1","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"40 mg","route":"Subcutaneous"},{"id":"admin_order_med_tdap_vaccine_2_d0","orderId":"order_med_tdap_vaccine_2","slotIndex":0,"time":"0900","state":"due","label":"0900 Due","dose":"0.5 mL","route":"Intramuscular"}],"devices":[],"ioEvents":[],"stickyNotes":[{"title":"Medication pass","body":"Scan the patient wristband first, then scan each medication. Check the five rights and the hold parameters before giving."}],"notes":[{"id":"note_nursing_admission_note_2026_10_20_07_21","type":"progressNotes","title":"Nursing Admission Note","author":"T. Nguyen, RN","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:21","category":"Nursing Note","summary":"Admission database and baseline assessment completed.","body":"**Admission assessment**\n- Arrived to the unit at 0645 from the ED. ID band and allergy band verified (No known drug allergies.).\n- Vitals on arrival: T 98.6 F, HR 84, BP 122/75, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10.\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds; left elbow: 3 cm superficial abrasion, clean, no drainage.\n- Pain 5/10; right hip, aching, 5/10 with movement.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds; left elbow: 3 cm superficial abrasion, clean, no drainage. Braden 21.\n- Fall risk: High; fall precautions in place.\n- Lines: none.\n\n**Education**\n- Oriented to room, call light, plan of care, and fall precautions.\n\n**Plan**"},{"id":"note_hospitalist_history_and_physical_2026_10_20_07_15","type":"hp","title":"Hospitalist History and Physical","author":"S. Patel, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 07:15","category":"H&P","summary":"Admission H&P for fall with right hip contusion and limited mobility.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fall at home with right hip pain\n\n**History of present illness**\n78-year-old female who slipped on a wet garage floor and landed on the right hip, scraping the left elbow. X-ray of the hip and pelvis shows no fracture. Bruising and tenderness over the right hip; walks only a few steps with a walker. Last tetanus shot more than 10 years ago. Admitted for observation, pain control, a tetanus booster, therapy and prevention of blood clots while mobility is limited.\n\n**Past medical history**\n- No significant past medical history.\n\n**Past surgical history**\n- No prior surgeries.\n\n**Home medications**\n- None\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Family history**\n- Mother with hypertension; father with coronary artery disease. No known family history of bowel disease or cancer.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Review of systems**\n- Positive for right hip pain, bruising and an elbow abrasion. Negative for head strike, loss of consciousness, chest pain, shortness of breath, bleeding or numbness.\n\n**Vitals**\n- T 98.6 F, HR 84, BP 122/75, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10 | Wt 64 kg, BMI 25.6\n\n**Physical exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds; left elbow: 3 cm superficial abrasion, clean, no drainage.\n\n**Data**\n- Labs: \n\n**Assessment and plan**\n78-year-old female with no significant history admitted with fall with right hip contusion and limited mobility.\n\n**Fall with right hip contusion and limited mobility**\n\n**Prophylaxis / code status**\n- DVT prophylaxis per orders; fall precautions.\n- Code status: Full Code."},{"id":"note_ed_provider_note_2026_10_20_06_03","type":"erVisitSummary","title":"ED Provider Note","author":"J. Whitaker, MD","datetime":"2026-10-20 06:03","category":"ED Note","summary":"78-year-old female presenting with fall at home with right hip pain; admitted to Hospital Medicine.","body":"**Chief complaint**\n- Fall at home with right hip pain\n\n**HPI**\n78-year-old female who slipped on a wet garage floor and landed on the right hip, scraping the left elbow. X-ray of the hip and pelvis shows no fracture. Bruising and tenderness over the right hip; walks only a few steps with a walker. Last tetanus shot more than 10 years ago. Admitted for observation, pain control, a tetanus booster, therapy and prevention of blood clots while mobility is limited.\n\n**Past medical / surgical history**\n- Medical: No significant past medical history.\n- Surgical: No prior surgeries.\n\n**Allergies**\n- No known drug allergies.\n\n**Social history**\n- Lives with spouse/partner; independent with ADLs and ambulation at baseline; tobacco: never; alcohol: none; other substances: none.\n\n**Triage vitals**\n- T 98.2 F, HR 84, BP 123/73, RR 16, SpO2 98% on room air, pain 5/10\n\n**Exam**\n- General: Awake and alert, in no acute distress.\n- Cardiovascular: Normal sinus rhythm; S1 S2 regular, no murmur. Edema: None.\n- Respiratory: Clear bilaterally; unlabored, even.\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, non-distended. Bowel sounds: active in all four quadrants.\n- Neurologic: Alert and oriented x4.\n- Skin: Right lateral hip: 10 x 8 cm bruise, tender, no open wounds; left elbow: 3 cm superficial abrasion, clean, no drainage.\n\n**ED results**\n- Labs: pending\n\n**ED course**\n- 0445 acetaminophen (TYLENOL) 650 mg Oral\n- 0445 enoxaparin (LOVENOX) 40 mg Subcutaneous\n- 0445 tetanus, diphtheria, pertussis vaccine (BOOSTRIX Tdap) 0.5 mL Intramuscular\n\n**Assessment / disposition**\n- Fall with right hip contusion and limited mobility. \n- Admit to Hospital Medicine (Dr. S. Patel); condition guarded but stable."}],"timeline":{"marDate":"Tuesday, October 20, 2026","marTimeSlots":["0800","0900","1000","1100","1200","1300","1400","1500"],"simulationStart":"2026-10-20 08:45","simulationEnd":"2026-10-20 16:45"},"simulationTasks":[],"triggers":[],"facultyBuilder":{"builderVersion":2,"inputs":{"name":"Dorothy Hughes","ag